  "id": "aps",
  "term": "APS",
  "definition": "APS refers to Astragalus polysaccharide, a biological substance studied for its effects on the gut microbiota and on glutamate/GABA-related metabolites. In this source, applying APS directly to the colon appeared to reduce microbiota and neuroactive-metabolite disruptions linked with major depressive disorder through the gut-brain axis.",
